        },
        {
          "id": "thm-fdmath-mean-fluctuation-energy-transfer",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Mean and fluctuation energy exchange",
          "reference": "items/thm-fdmath-mean-fluctuation-energy-transfer.md",
          "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "thm-fdmath-finite-reynolds-identity"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-fdmath-finite-reynolds-identity": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open interval, let $d\\ge2$ and $N\\ge1$ be integers, and define the flat torus $\\mathbb T^d:=(\\mathbb R/2\\pi\\mathbb Z)^d$, with integration using Lebesgue measure on a periodic cell $[0,2\\pi]^d$. Fix constants $a_j\\ge0$ with $\\sum_{j=1}^N a_j=1$ and a common constant $\\nu\\ge0$. For $j=1,\\ldots,N$, let $u_j:I\\times\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be continuously differentiable in $(t,x)$ with continuous second spatial derivatives, and let $p_j:I\\times\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuously differentiable. Require these fields to be $2\\pi$-periodic in each spatial coordinate, so they descend to $\\mathbb T^d$. Suppose they are unforced and satisfy pointwise on $I\\times\\mathbb R^d$\n\n$$\\operatorname{div}u_j=0,\\qquad \\partial_tu_j+\\operatorname{div}(u_j\\otimes u_j)+\\nabla p_j=\\nu\\Delta u_j.$$\n\nUse $(u\\otimes v)_{rs}=u_rv_s$, $(\\operatorname{div}A)_r=\\sum_s\\partial_{x_s}A_{rs}$ for a matrix field $A$, and componentwise Laplacian. For $A\\in\\mathbb R^{d\\times d}$ set $\\operatorname{tr}A:=\\sum_rA_{rr}$. Define $\\bar u=\\sum_j a_ju_j$, $v_j=u_j-\\bar u$, $R=\\sum_j a_jv_j\\otimes v_j$, and\n\n$$E_m(t):=\\frac12\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}|\\bar u(t,x)|^2\\,dx,\\qquad E_f(t):=\\frac12\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}\\operatorname{tr}R(t,x)\\,dx=\\frac12\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}\\sum_j a_j|v_j(t,x)|^2\\,dx.$$\n\nFor a matrix $A$ and vector field $q$, set $A:\\nabla q:=\\sum_{r,s=1}^d A_{rs}\\partial_{x_s}q_r$ and $|\\nabla q|^2:=\\sum_{r,s=1}^d|\\partial_{x_s}q_r|^2$. Then for every $t\\in I$,\n\n$$\\frac{dE_m}{dt}=-\\nu\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}|\\nabla\\bar u|^2\\,dx+\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}R:\\nabla\\bar u\\,dx,$$\n\n$$\\frac{dE_f}{dt}=-\\nu\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}\\sum_j a_j|\\nabla v_j|^2\\,dx-\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}R:\\nabla\\bar u\\,dx.$$\n\nFor every $t_0<t_1$ in $I$, the endpoint identities are\n\n$$E_m(t_1)-E_m(t_0)=-\\nu\\int_{t_0}^{t_1}\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}|\\nabla\\bar u|^2\\,dx\\,dt+\\int_{t_0}^{t_1}\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}R:\\nabla\\bar u\\,dx\\,dt,$$\n\n$$E_f(t_1)-E_f(t_0)=-\\nu\\int_{t_0}^{t_1}\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}\\sum_j a_j|\\nabla v_j|^2\\,dx\\,dt-\\int_{t_0}^{t_1}\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}R:\\nabla\\bar u\\,dx\\,dt.$$\n\nThe transfer term has opposite signs in the two balances and cancels in their sum. No sign is asserted for $\\int_{\\mathbb T^d}R:\\nabla\\bar u\\,dx$.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-altered",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
