          "id": "cex-fdmath-mean-does-not-determine-covariance",
          "kind": "counterexample",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Equal means with unequal Reynolds covariance",
          "reference": "items/cex-fdmath-mean-does-not-determine-covariance.md",
          "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "thm-fdmath-finite-reynolds-identity"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "thm-fdmath-finite-reynolds-identity": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Fix any integer $d\\ge2$ and any $\\nu\\ge0$, and define $\\mathbb T^d=(\\mathbb R/2\\pi\\mathbb Z)^d$. Consider the entire class of finite ensembles described as follows, allowing the number of members and the weight tuple to vary across the class. Each ensemble has an integer $N\\ge1$ and fixed weights $a_j\\ge0$ with $\\sum_{j=1}^N a_j=1$. For $j=1,\\ldots,N$, let $u_j:\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be continuously differentiable in $(t,x)$ with continuous second spatial derivatives, and let $p_j:\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuously differentiable. Require all these fields to be $2\\pi$-periodic in each spatial coordinate, and suppose that for each $j=1,\\ldots,N$, pointwise on $\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^d$,\n\n$$\\operatorname{div}u_j=0,\\qquad \\partial_tu_j+\\operatorname{div}(u_j\\otimes u_j)+\\nabla p_j=\\nu\\Delta u_j.$$\n\nFor each such family, define $\\bar u=\\sum_j a_ju_j$, $\\bar p=\\sum_j a_jp_j$, and $R=\\sum_j a_j(u_j-\\bar u)\\otimes(u_j-\\bar u)$. The following universal determination assertion over this entire class is false: any two ensembles in the class with the same mean velocity and mean pressure fields $\\bar u,\\bar p$ must have the same covariance tensor $R$.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "ai-generated",
            "proof": "ai-generated"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Glenn Flierl and Raffaele Ferrari, MIT OpenCourseWare 12.820, Turbulence in the Ocean and Atmosphere, Chapter 3, §3.6 (Spring 2006 lecture notes)",
                "url": "https://www.ocw.mit.edu/courses/12-820-turbulence-in-the-ocean-and-atmosphere-spring-2006/a3ea9a7900aee9c9ebaf444ab2d92c1a_ch3.pdf"
              }
            ]
          },
          "library": "mathematics",
          "proof_strategy": "direct",
          "generation": {
            "role": "counterexample"
          }
        }
      ],
