          "statement": "On the periodic interface $x\\in\\mathbb T_{2\\pi}$, where $\\mathbb T_{2\\pi}=\\mathbb R/(2\\pi\\mathbb Z)$, with half-planes $y>0$ and $y<0$, take equal density $\\rho_0=1$, base velocities $U_+=1$ and $U_-=-1$, and no gravity or surface tension. For $t\\ge0$, define\n$$\\eta(x,t)=e^t\\cos x,\\qquad \\phi_+(x,y,t)=e^{t-y}(\\sin x-\\cos x),\\qquad \\phi_-(x,y,t)=e^{t+y}(\\cos x+\\sin x).$$\nThe potentials are harmonic and decay at their respective infinities; at $y=0$ they satisfy $(\\partial_t+U_\\pm\\partial_x)\\eta=\\partial_y\\phi_\\pm$ and continuity of $p'_\\pm=-(\\partial_t+U_\\pm\\partial_x)\\phi_\\pm$. Thus these fields give an exact real growing mode of the stipulated linear interface equations.",
