          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Assume countable choice: every countable family of nonempty sets has a choice function. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open interval, let $C_0\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be a bounded open region with $C^1$ boundary (locally a $C^1$ graph with the region on one side), and let $U_C$ be an open neighborhood of $\\overline{C_0}$. Let $X\\in C^2(I\\times U_C;\\mathbb R^3)$ have orientation-preserving diffeomorphic time slices onto open images (bijections with $C^2$ inverses and positive Jacobian determinant). Here $C^r$ means all coordinate partial derivatives through order $r$ are continuous, and set $C(t)=X_t(C_0)$. Let $g$ be a scalar $C^1$ field on an open neighborhood of $\\{(t,x):x\\in\\overline{C(t)},\\,t\\in I\\}$. Define the boundary velocity by $w(t,X(t,\\xi))=\\partial_tX(t,\\xi)$ and let $n$ be the outward Euclidean unit normal on $\\partial C(t)$. Use Euclidean surface measure, whose chart density is $\\sqrt{\\det(DY^{\\mathsf T}DY)}$. Then\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{C(t)}g(t,x)\\,dx =\\int_{C(t)}\\partial_tg(t,x)\\,dx+\\int_{\\partial C(t)}g(t,x)\\,w(t,x)\\cdot n(t,x)\\,dS_x.$$\nFor vector-valued $g$, the identity holds componentwise. No condition equating $w$ with a fluid velocity is required.",
