          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be an open interval containing $0$, let $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be a bounded open reference region with $C^1$ boundary (locally a $C^1$ graph with the region on one side), and let $U$ be an open neighborhood of $\\overline B$. Let $\\chi\\in C^2(I\\times U;\\mathbb R^3)$ have orientation-preserving diffeomorphic time slices (bijections onto open images with $C^2$ inverses and positive Jacobian determinant), and satisfy $\\chi(0,a)=a$. Here $C^r$ means all coordinate partial derivatives through order $r$ are continuous; write $\\Omega_t=\\chi_t(B)$ and $u(t,\\chi(t,a))=\\partial_t\\chi(t,a)$. Let $\\rho_0\\in C^1(\\overline B)$ and $\\rho\\in C^1(\\mathcal O)$ be positive mass densities, where $\\mathcal O=\\{(t,x):t\\in I,\\ x\\in\\chi_t(U)\\}$. Suppose that for every nonempty bounded open $V$ with compact closure in $B$ and $C^1$ boundary locally a graph with the region on one side and every $t\\in I$,\n$$\\int_{\\chi_t(V)}\\rho(t,x)\\,dx=\\int_V\\rho_0(a)\\,da.$$\nThen the pointwise continuity equation\n$$\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}_x(\\rho u)=0$$\nholds throughout the balanced physical region $\\mathcal O_B:=\\{(t,x):t\\in I,\\ x\\in\\chi_t(B)\\}$. The larger set $\\mathcal O$ is only the ambient regularity domain; no balance outside $\\chi_t(B)$ is assumed or concluded. This is a conditional deduction in the smooth material model and asserts no extension to weak fields or vacuum.",
