hi(s,a))\\in\\mathcal O$ and $u(t_0+s,\\chi(s,a))=\\partial_s\\chi(s,a)$ for all $s\\in K,a\\in U_B$. Write $\\widetilde f(s,x):=f(t_0+s,x)$ for each field $f$. For every nonempty bounded open $V\\Subset B$ with one-sided $C^1$ graph boundary, put $P_s=\\chi_s(V)$ and let $\\nu$ be its outward unit normal. Require\n\n$$\\int_{P_s}\\widetilde\\rho\\,dx=\\int_V\\rho(t_0,a)\\,da,\\qquad \\frac{d}{ds}\\int_{P_s}\\widetilde\\rho\\widetilde u\\,dx=\\int_{P_s}\\widetilde\\rho\\widetilde b\\,dx+\\int_{\\partial P_s}\\widetilde\\sigma\\nu\\,dS.$$\n\nAssume also the Axiom of Choice. These material charts may depend on $(t_0,x_0)$; no global material chart or angular or total-energy balance is required.\n\nThen every such $C(t)$ satisfies\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{C(t)}\\rho\\,dx=-\\int_{\\partial C(t)}\\rho\\,(u-w)\\cdot n\\,dS,$$\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\int_{C(t)}\\rho u\\,dx=\\int_{C(t)}\\rho b\\,dx+\\int_{\\partial C(t)}\\sigma n\\,dS-\\int_{\\partial C(t)}\\rho u\\,\\bigl((u-w)\\cdot n\\bigr)\\,dS.$$\n\nOnly the normal component $w\\cdot n$ enters these balances. If $C(t)$ is material, so $w\\cdot n=u\\cdot n$ on its boundary, the relative mass and advective-momentum fluxes vanish. The conclusion is a conditional model deduction; it asserts no existence of a flow satisfying the balances.",
