          "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice: every set-indexed family of nonempty sets has a choice function. Let $L_1,L_2,L_3>0$ be side lengths in metres and let $Q:=\\prod_{j=1}^3[0,L_j]$ be a periodic cell, with opposite faces identified as in the periodic boundary-data model. Let $\\rho>0$ be constant mass density in kilograms per cubic metre, $c>0$ constant specific heat in joules per kilogram kelvin, $\\kappa>0$ constant thermal conductivity in watts per metre kelvin, $T_*>|a|>0$ a reference temperature and amplitude in kelvins, and $m\\in\\mathbb Z^3\\setminus\\{0\\}$. Put $k_j:=2\\pi m_j/L_j$ in inverse metres, define $k:=(k_1,k_2,k_3)\\in\\mathbb R^3$, and put $\\lambda:=\\kappa|k|^2/(\\rho c)$ in inverse seconds. Choose $0<\\delta<\\lambda^{-1}\\log(T_*/|a|)$, put $I:=(-\\delta,\\infty)$, and, for $(t,x)\\in I\\times\\mathbb R^3$, define\n\n$$T(t,x):=T_*+a e^{-\\lambda t}\\cos(k\\cdot x),\\qquad u:=0,\\quad \\sigma:=0,\\quad b:=0,\\quad r:=0,\\quad q:=-\\kappa\\nabla T,$$\n\n$$e:=cT,\\qquad s:=c\\log(T/T_*).$$\n\nThen $T>0$, these fields satisfy the smooth balance equations on the periodic cell, and total internal energy $\\int_Q\\rho e\\,dx$ is constant. The physical entropy density satisfies\n\n$$\\partial_t(\\rho s)+\\operatorname{div}(q/T)=\\kappa\\frac{|\\nabla T|^2}{T^2}\\ge0,$$\n\nand the total entropy $\\int_Q\\rho s\\,dx$ is strictly increasing for every finite $t\\ge0$. This is an exact conditional calculation for the stated balance-law and caloric model; it is not an experimental observation or a constitutive claim about a particular substance.",
