          "statement": "Assume the complete smooth material, state, contact and mass/momentum/angular-momentum/total-energy balance hypotheses of the local Gibbs-entropy identity, including $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ and positive temperature, as stated in Facts & Assumptions. Use a $C^2$ local state relation $e(v,s)$ with $v=1/\\rho$, $T=e_s(v,s)>0$, and $p=-e_v(v,s)$. Let $\\sigma=-pI_3+\\tau$, define $L_{ij}=\\partial_{x_j}u_i$, $D=(L+L^T)/2$, $\\theta=\\operatorname{tr}D$, and set\n$$ \\mathcal G=\\rho D_ts+\\operatorname{div}(q/T)-\\rho r/T,\\qquad D_t=\\partial_t+u\\cdot\\nabla. $$\nFor the adopted Newtonian/Fourier form $\\tau=2\\mu D_0+\\zeta\\theta I_3$, define $D_0=D-\\theta I_3/3$, $A:B:=\\sum_{i,j=1}^3A_{ij}B_{ij}$ for $A,B\\in\\mathbb R^{3\\times3}$, and $|D_0|^2:=D_0:D_0=\\sum_{i,j=1}^3(D_0)_{ij}^2$. Set $\\operatorname{sym}(K):=(K+K^T)/2$ and $q=-K\\nabla T$. The residual is\n$$ \\mathcal G=\\frac{2\\mu|D_0|^2+\\zeta\\theta^2}{T} +\\frac{(\\nabla T)^T\\operatorname{sym}(K)\\nabla T}{T^2}. $$\nAt a fixed state, if the algebraic coefficient family is tested for every symmetric $D$, every $g=\\nabla T\\in\\mathbb R^3$, and every $T>0$, this residual is nonnegative exactly when $\\mu\\ge0$, $\\zeta\\ge0$, and $x^T\\operatorname{sym}(K)x\\ge0$ for every $x\\in\\mathbb R^3$. These conditions make the adopted closure compatible with the separate continuum entropy inequality. In SI units, $\\mathcal G$ has units $\\mathrm{W\\,m^{-3}\\,K^{-1}}$. The theorem does not derive the balance or entropy postulates, infer material coefficients, or assert empirical validity.",
