        {
          "id": "thm-fd-global-linear-acoustics",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "domain": "mathematics",
          "title": "Global smooth periodic linear acoustics",
          "reference": "items/thm-fd-global-linear-acoustics.md",
          "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; conditional interfaces and source scope are recorded in batch-18 notes.",
          "dependency_level": 2,
          "deps": [
            "def-fd-periodic-fourier-sobolev-spaces",
            "thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus",
            "lem-fd-periodic-fourier-embedding-products",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "dependency_roles": {
            "def-fd-periodic-fourier-sobolev-spaces": "mathematical-premise",
            "thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus": "mathematical-premise",
            "lem-fd-periodic-fourier-embedding-products": "mathematical-premise",
            "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
          },
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$, $\\rho_*>0$, $c_*>0$, and let $z_0:\\mathbb T^d\\to\\mathbb R$ and $v_0:\\mathbb T^d\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be smooth periodic data on the normalized torus $\\mathbb T^d=(\\mathbb R/2\\pi\\mathbb Z)^d$. Use normalized measure $d\\mu=(2\\pi)^{-d}dx$, coefficients $\\widehat f(k)=\\int f(x)e^{-ik\\cdot x}\\,d\\mu(x)$, weights $w_k=(1+|k|^2)^{1/2}$, and componentwise norms $\\|f\\|_{H^m}^2=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^d}w_k^{2m}|\\widehat f(k)|^2$. To define the tangent system, let $P:(0,\\infty)\\to\\mathbb R$ be any $C^2$ function with $P^{\\prime}(\\rho_*)=c_*^2$ (for example, $P(\\rho)=c_*^2\\rho$). The base nonlinear equations are $\\rho_t+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u)=0$ and $u_t+u\\cdot\\nabla u+\\rho^{-1}\\nabla P(\\rho)=0$, for smooth positive scalar $\\rho$ and vector $u$ on spacetime. The equilibrium is $(\\rho,u)=(\\rho_*,0)$. By its tangent system we mean that the derivative at $\\epsilon=0$ of each equation residual evaluated at $(\\rho,u)=(\\rho_*+\\epsilon z,\\epsilon v)$ vanishes; the perturbation fields are arbitrary smooth maps, and $\\epsilon$ is restricted near zero on each compact time interval so that density stays positive. The resulting constant-coefficient tangent system\n$$z_t+\\rho_*\\operatorname{div}v=0,\\qquad v_t+(c_*^2/\\rho_*)\\nabla z=0,\\qquad (z,v)|_{t=0}=(z_0,v_0)$$\nhas a unique real $C^\\infty$ solution $(z,v)$ on $\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb T^d$. For every integer $m\\ge0$, the weighted energy $\\|v(t)\\|_{H^m}^2+(c_*^2/\\rho_*^2)\\|z(t)\\|_{H^m}^2$ is constant for all $t\\in\\mathbb R$. This is the exact linear tangent model; it does not assert equality with a finite-amplitude nonlinear fluid evolution.",
