          },
          "statement": "Let $N\\ge1$, let $F:\\mathbb R^N\\to\\mathbb R^N$ be a polynomial map, and let $T_*>0$. If $x\\in C^1([0,T_*),\\mathbb R^N)$ solves $x'(t)=F(x(t))$ and there is $R\\ge0$ such that $\\|x(t)\\|_2\\le R$ for every $0\\le t<T_*$, then there are $\\epsilon>0$ and a solution $\\widetilde x\\in C^1([0,T_*+\\epsilon),\\mathbb R^N)$ of the same ODE with $\\widetilde x(t)=x(t)$ for $0\\le t<T_*$. Thus a finite right endpoint of a bounded finite-dimensional polynomial ODE trajectory is extendible.",
