          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$, $\\kappa>0$, $\\gamma>1$, $a=(\\gamma-1)/2$, integer $s\\ge4$, and smooth real periodic maps $\\rho_0:\\mathbb T^d\\to(0,\\infty)$ and $u_0:\\mathbb T^d\\to\\mathbb R^d$, where $\\mathbb T^d=(\\mathbb R/2\\pi\\mathbb Z)^d$, with $\\min_{x\\in\\mathbb T^d}\\rho_0(x)>0$. Use normalized measure $d\\mu=(2\\pi)^{-d}dx$, coefficients $\\widehat f(k)=\\int f(x)e^{-ik\\cdot x}\\,d\\mu(x)$, weights $w_k=(1+|k|^2)^{1/2}$, and componentwise norms $\\|f\\|_{H^m}^2=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^d}w_k^{2m}|\\widehat f(k)|^2$. For $\\rho>0$, set $p(\\rho)=\\kappa\\rho^\\gamma$ and $r(\\rho)=\\sqrt{\\kappa\\gamma}\\,\\rho^a/a$. Then there is $T>0$, depending only on $d,s,\\kappa,\\gamma$, $\\|(r(\\rho_0),u_0)\\|_{H^s}$, and $\\min r(\\rho_0)$, and a unique smooth real solution $(\\rho,u)$ on $[0,T]\\times\\mathbb T^d$ of\n$$\\rho_t+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u)=0,\\qquad u_t+u\\cdot\\nabla u+\\rho^{-1}\\nabla(\\kappa\\rho^\\gamma)=0,$$\nwith initial data $(\\rho_0,u_0)$ and $\\rho(t,x)>0$. For every integer $m\\ge s$, $\\sup_{0\\le t\\le T}(\\|\\rho(t)\\|_{H^m}+\\|u(t)\\|_{H^m})<\\infty$. This conditional smooth periodic theorem concerns the isentropic barotropic model with strictly positive density; it asserts no continuation through vacuum or shocks and no viscous or temperature-coupled result.",
