          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\ell,\\rho_*,\\eta,\\kappa>0$, $\\gamma>1$, $\\zeta\\ge0$, and $A\\in\\mathbb R$. On $\\mathbb T^3_\\ell=(\\mathbb R/2\\pi\\ell\\mathbb Z)^3$ with coordinates $(x,y,z)$, set $\\nu=\\eta/\\rho_*$, $p_*=\\kappa\\rho_*^\\gamma$, and $V(t,y)=Ae^{-\\nu t/\\ell^2}\\sin(y/\\ell)$. Then $\\rho=\\rho_*$ and $u=(V,0,0)$ give a global smooth solution with no external force of\n$$\\rho_t+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u)=0,\\qquad (\\rho u)_t+\\operatorname{div}(\\rho u\\otimes u)+\\nabla(\\kappa\\rho^\\gamma)=\\operatorname{div}\\!\\left(2\\eta D_0+\\zeta(\\operatorname{div}u)I\\right),$$\nwhere $D_0=(\\nabla u+\\nabla u^{\\mathsf T})/2-(\\operatorname{div}u)I/3$. This is the first sine heat mode of the compatible channel shear evolution at channel height $h=\\pi\\ell$, periodically extended in $y$. It is one exact solution of the compressible viscous system, not a general nonconstant-density existence result. With SI units, $x,y,z,\\ell$ are metres, $t$ is seconds, $A,u$ are m/s, $\\rho_*$ is kg/m$^3$, $p_*$ is Pa, $\\eta,\\zeta$ are Pa$\\cdot$s, $\\kappa$ is Pa$\\cdot$(m$^3$/kg)$^\\gamma$, and $\\nu$ is m$^2$/s.",
