          "inventory_expansion_required": false,
          "statement": "Let $v,w,v\\prime,w\\prime\\in\\mathbb R^3$ be velocities measured in metres per second, let $dv$ be three-dimensional Lebesgue measure, and set $Q_{\\rm el}:=\\{(v,w,v\\prime,w\\prime):v+w=v\\prime+w\\prime,\\ |v|^2+|w|^2=|v\\prime|^2+|w\\prime|^2\\}$. Let $\\nu$ be a nonnegative countably additive measure on $Q_{\\rm el}$ invariant under exchange of either velocity pair and interchange of incoming and outgoing pairs. For a positive finite-valued Lebesgue-measurable velocity density $g\\in L^1(\\mathbb R^3)$ whose four coordinate evaluations on $Q_{\\rm el}$ are $\\nu$-measurable, set $A_g:=g(v)g(w)$ and $B_g:=g(v\\prime)g(w\\prime)$, and define the possibly infinite collision entropy production by $\\mathscr P_\\nu(g):=\\frac14\\int_{Q_{\\rm el}}(A_g-B_g)\\log(A_g/B_g)\\,d\\nu$. A Maxwellian means a function $C\\exp(-|v-U|^2/(2\\theta))$ for a density scale $C>0$ with the units of $g$, a velocity $U\\in\\mathbb R^3$, and squared speed $\\theta>0$. Full support means every nonempty relatively open subset of $Q_{\\rm el}$ has positive $\\nu$-measure. The proposed implication that $\\mathscr P_\\nu(g)=0$ forces $g$ to be Maxwellian for every such symmetric $\\nu$ and positive integrable $g$ is false without a full-support assumption on $\\nu$.",
