          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$: every $\\mathbb N$-indexed family of nonempty sets has a choice function. Let $\\Omega=\\prod_{j=1}^3(\\mathbb R/L_j\\mathbb Z)$ be a fixed rectangular periodic cell with periods $L_j>0$ in metres, $T_*>0$ in seconds, and $\\varepsilon>0$ a dimensionless fast-collision parameter. Spatial position $x$ is measured in metres, velocity $v$ in metres per second, and $f^\\varepsilon d^3x\\,d^3v$ counts particles, so $f^\\varepsilon$ has units $\\mathrm{s^3\\,m^{-6}}$. Put $v_*=1\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ and $\\omega_k(v)=\\sum_{j=0}^k(|v|/v_*)^j$ for $k=2,3$. For each $\\varepsilon$, let $f^\\varepsilon>0$ be periodic on $\\Omega$, continuously differentiable in $t,x$, and twice continuously differentiable in $v$ on $\\Omega\\times\\mathbb R^3\\times[0,T_*]$. Let $f_{\\rm ref}>0$ be constant in the same units as $f^\\varepsilon$ and put $\\ell^\\varepsilon=\\log(f^\\varepsilon/f_{\\rm ref})$. On each compact time interval, require integrable velocity majorants uniform in $x,t$ for each of $\\omega_3 f^\\varepsilon$, $\\omega_3|\\partial_t f^\\varepsilon|$, $\\omega_3|v\\cdot\\nabla_xf^\\varepsilon|$, $f^\\varepsilon|\\ell^\\varepsilon|$, $|v|f^\\varepsilon|\\ell^\\varepsilon|$, $(1+|\\ell^\\varepsilon|)|\\partial_t f^\\varepsilon|$, and $(1+|\\ell^\\varepsilon|)|v||\\nabla_x f^\\varepsilon|$. Require the collision logarithmic test to be absolutely integrable. Define\n\n$$Q_{\\rm el}=\\{(v,w,v',w')\\in(\\mathbb R^3)^4:v+w=v'+w',\\ |v|^2+|w|^2=|v'|^2+|w'|^2\\}$$\n\nwith its relative Borel sigma-algebra and let $\\nu$ be the nonnegative symmetric collision-rate measure on this set. For each admissible velocity test $\\psi$ with absolute convergence, the collision operator is assumed to satisfy\n\n$$\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\psi(v)Q_\\nu(f^\\varepsilon)(x,v,t)\\,d^3v=\\frac14\\int_{Q_{\\rm el}}(B-A)\\bigl(\\psi(v)+\\psi(w)-\\psi(v')-\\psi(w')\\bigr)\\,d\\nu,$$\n\nwhere $A=f^\\varepsilon(x,v,t)f^\\varepsilon(x,w,t)$ and $B=f^\\varepsilon(x,v',t)f^\\varepsilon(x,w',t)$. In particular require this identity for $\\psi=1,mv_i,m|v|^2/2$; the elastic collision constraints make each corresponding collision bracket zero. Require $f^\\varepsilon$ to solve\n\n$$\\varepsilon\\bigl(\\partial_t f^\\varepsilon+v\\cdot\\nabla_x f^\\varepsilon\\bigr)=Q_\\nu(f^\\varepsilon),$$\n\nLet $m>0$ in kilograms and $k_B>0$ in joules per kelvin. Let $n,u,T$ be $C^1$ periodic fields, with $n,T$ bounded above and bounded away from zero and $u$ bounded, and define their local Maxwellian by\n\n$$M_{n,u,T}(v)=n\\left(\\frac{m}{2\\pi k_BT}\\right)^{3/2}\\exp\\left(-\\frac{m|v-u|^2}{2k_BT}\\right),$$\n\nwhere $n$ is number density in $\\mathrm{m^{-3}}$, $u$ is velocity in $\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$, $T$ is translational temperature in kelvins, $p$ is pressure in pascals ($\\mathrm{J\\,m^{-3}}$), and $I_3$ below is the identity tensor on $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nFor the fixed velocity unit $v_*=1\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$, assume\n\n$$\\int_0^{T_*}\\int_\\Omega\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\omega_3(v)|f^\\varepsilon-M_{n,u,T}|\\,d^3v\\,d^3x\\,dt\\longrightarrow0\\quad\\text{as }\\varepsilon\\to0,$$\n\nand assume the initial convergence\n\n$$\\int_\\Omega\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\omega_2(v)|f^\\varepsilon(x,v,0)-M_{n(x,0),u(x,0),T(x,0)}(v)|\\,d^3v\\,d^3x\\longrightarrow0.$$\n\nThen, with $\\rho=mn$, $E=\\frac12\\rho|u|^2+\\frac32nk_BT$, and local-equilibrium scalar pressure $p=nk_BT$, the limiting fields satisfy the compressible ideal-monatomic-gas Euler equations\n\n$$\\partial_t\\rho+\\nabla_x\\cdot(\\rho u)=0,$$\n\n$$\\partial_t(\\rho u)+\\nabla_x\\cdot(\\rho u\\otimes u+pI_3)=0,$$\n\n$$\\partial_tE+\\nabla_x\\cdot((E+p)u)=0.$$\n\nThe equations hold distributionally and pointwise because the limiting fields are $C^1$; the initial trace is the one supplied by the initial convergence. The weighted strong convergence is a hypothesis, not a consequence of small $\\varepsilon$, the entropy estimate, or the adopted model alone. This i