          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Bounded Stokes pressure sensors",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$ and let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected Lipschitz open set. Put $Q:=L^2_0(D)=\\{q\\in L^2(D;\\mathbb R):\\int_Dq\\,dx=0\\}$ with the $L^2$ norm, and write $Q'$ for the continuous real dual of $Q$. A bounded Stokes pressure sensor on $D$ is a bounded real-linear functional $S:Q\\to\\mathbb R$, where bounded means that its operator norm $\\|S\\|_{Q'}:=\\sup_{\\|q\\|_{L^2(D)}\\le1}|S(q)|$ is finite. The reading of $S$ at a normalized pressure $q\\in Q$ is $S(q)$.",
