          "id": "thm-fd-stokes-load-observable-stability",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "Lipschitz stability of bounded Stokes pressure observations",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$, let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected Lipschitz open set, and let $\\nu>0$. Set $V=H^1_0(D;\\mathbb R^d)$ with $\\|v\\|_V=\\|\\nabla v\\|_{L^2(D)}$ and $Q=L^2_0(D)$ with the $L^2$ norm. For each $F\\in V'$, let $(u_F,p_F)\\in V\\times Q$ be the unique pair satisfying\n$$2\\nu\\int_D\\varepsilon(u_F):\\varepsilon(v)\\,dx-\\int_Dp_F\\,\\operatorname{div}v\\,dx=F(v)\\quad(v\\in V),\\qquad-\\int_Dq\\,\\operatorname{div}u_F\\,dx=0\\quad(q\\in Q),$$\nwhere $V'$ is the continuous real dual of $V$ and $\\varepsilon(u)=(\\nabla u+\\nabla u^T)/2$. Write $C_{\\rm div}(D)$ for a finite constant in a bounded right inverse estimate $\\operatorname{div}B_Dq=q$ and $\\|\\nabla B_Dq\\|_{L^2(D)}\\le C_{\\rm div}(D)\\|q\\|_{L^2(D)}$ for $q\\in Q$. For a positive integer $m$ and bounded pressure sensors $S_1,\\ldots,S_m\\in Q'$, define $\\mathcal O(F)=(S_1(p_F),\\ldots,S_m(p_F))\\in\\mathbb R^m$. Then $F\\mapsto p_F$ and $\\mathcal O$ are real-linear, and for all $F,G\\in V'$\n$$\\|\\mathcal O(F)-\\mathcal O(G)\\|_{\\mathbb R^m}\\le 3C_{\\rm div}(D)\\left(\\sum_{j=1}^m\\|S_j\\|_{Q'}^2\\right)^{1/2}\\|F-G\\|_{V'},$$\nwhere $\\mathbb R^m$ has its Euclidean norm.",
