          "id": "prop-fd-pressure-gauge-observables",
          "kind": "proposition",
          "title": "Gauge-invariant pressure sensor weights",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$ and let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected Lipschitz open set, with $V=H^1_0(D;\\mathbb R^d)$ and $Q=L^2_0(D)$. Take $g\\in L^2(D;\\mathbb R)$ and define $S_g(q):=\\int_Dgq\\,dx$ for $q\\in Q$; this is a bounded pressure sensor. Put $\\bar g:=|D|^{-1}\\int_Dg\\,dx$. On the normalized pressure space, $S_g=S_{g-\\bar g}$. Whenever $p$ denotes an unnormalized pressure representative in a weak pressure term or sensor reading below, take $p\\in L^2(D;\\mathbb R)$; a normalized pressure is denoted $q\\in Q\\subset L^2(D;\\mathbb R)$. The weak Stokes pressure term $-\\int_Dp\\,\\operatorname{div}v\\,dx$ is unchanged by $p\\mapsto p+c$ for $v\\in V$ and $c\\in\\mathbb R$. The unnormalized sensor reading $\\int_Dgp\\,dx$ is unchanged under every pressure shift $p\\mapsto p+c$ if and only if $\\int_Dg\\,dx=0$, equivalently $g\\in Q$.",
