          "title": "Bounded velocity-observation error for the smooth MINI branch",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and a smooth MINI observation interface as specified by the interface definition on this page. In particular, let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be bounded, connected, Lipschitz and polygonal or polyhedral with $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$; use a shape-regular conforming affine simplicial mesh, viscosity $\\nu>0$, $f\\in L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)$, the mass-projected initial value, and any actual mixed backward Euler MINI solution. Suppose the exact no-slip solution has $u\\in W^{1,\\infty}(0,T;H^2(D)^d\\cap V_\\sigma)$ and $p\\in W^{1,\\infty}(0,T;H^1(D)\\cap L^2_0(D))$. Set\n$$M=1+\\|u\\|_{W^{1,\\infty}H^2}+\\|p\\|_{W^{1,\\infty}H^1},\\qquad H=hM+\\tau_{\\max}M^2,\\qquad M_u=\\|u\\|_{L^\\infty(0,T;V)},\\qquad \\Lambda=1+C_D\\nu^{-3}M_u^4.$$\nAssume $\\tau_{\\max}\\Lambda\\le\\tfrac12$. Let $M_\\infty$, $M_E$ and $C_*$ have exactly the values in the smooth MINI velocity-error estimate, namely\n$$M_\\infty=\\bigl(\\|u(0)\\|_2^2+C_P(D)^2\\nu^{-1}\\|f\\|_{L^2L^2}^2\\bigr)^{1/2},\\qquad M_E=\\nu^{-1/2}\\|u(0)\\|_2+C_P(D)\\nu^{-1}\\|f\\|_{L^2L^2},$$\n$$C_*=C_{D,\\mathrm{shape}}(1+\\nu)^2(1+\\nu^{-4})(1+T)^2(1+M_\\infty+M_E+M)^4\\exp(2T\\Lambda),$$\nwhere $C_D$ depends only on the domain, dimension and trilinear-form constant, and $C_{D,\\mathrm{shape}}$ is independent of $h$, the time steps and $\\nu$. No mesh/time coupling is imposed beyond the stated time-step restriction. For any sensors $\\ell_n\\in V^*$, define $\\|\\ell\\|_{\\ell^2_\\tau(V^*)}=(\\sum_{n=1}^N\\tau_n\\|\\ell_n\\|_{V^*}^2)^{1/2}$. Then the endpoint-sampled observations of the interface satisfy\n$$\\left|\\mathcal O_h(\\ell;u_h)-\\mathcal O(\\ell;u)\\right|\\le \\nu^{-1/2}C_*H\\,\\|\\ell\\|_{\\ell^2_\\tau(V^*)}.$$\nThis is a conditional bound for bounded linear velocity sensors on the smooth branch; it makes no Reynolds-uniform claim.",
