          "title": "Accumulated pressure-observation error for the smooth MINI branch",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and a smooth MINI observation interface as specified by the interface definition on this page. In particular, $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ is bounded, connected, Lipschitz and polygonal or polyhedral with $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$; $T>0$, $\\nu>0$, and $f\\in L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)$; the exact no-slip solution has $u\\in W^{1,\\infty}(0,T;H^2(D)^d\\cap V_\\sigma)$ and $p\\in W^{1,\\infty}(0,T;H^1(D)\\cap Q)$; the MINI meshes are shape-regular conforming affine simplices; the initial value is $u_h^0=P_{Z_h}u(0)$; and any actual mixed backward Euler MINI solution is used. No mesh/time relation is imposed. Impose the time-step restriction $\\tau_{\\max}\\Lambda\\le\\tfrac12$ of the smooth-branch pressure-primitive theorem. Set $M=1+\\|u\\|_{W^{1,\\infty}H^2}+\\|p\\|_{W^{1,\\infty}H^1}$, $H=hM+\\tau_{\\max}M^2$, $M_u=\\|u\\|_{L^\\infty(0,T;V)}$, $M_E=\\nu^{-1/2}\\|u(0)\\|_2+C_P(D)\\nu^{-1}\\|f\\|_{L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)}$, and $\\Lambda=1+C_D\\nu^{-3}M_u^4$, where $C_D$ depends only on the domain, dimension and trilinear-form constant. Let $C_*$ be exactly the explicit viscosity-dependent constant in the smooth MINI velocity-error theorem. Let $\\beta>0$ be the uniform MINI inf-sup lower bound, let $M_b=\\sqrt d$, let $C_I$ be a mean-adjusted continuous P1 pressure interpolation constant satisfying $\\inf_{q_h\\in Q_h}\\|q-q_h\\|_2\\le C_Ih\\|q\\|_{H^1(D)}$ for $q\\in H^1(D)\\cap Q$, and choose $C_c$ such that $|c(a;b,v)|\\le C_c\\|a\\|_V\\|b\\|_V\\|v\\|_V$. Let $C_P(D)$ satisfy $\\|v\\|_{L^2(D)}\\le C_P(D)\\|v\\|_V$ for $v\\in V$. With\n$$K=(1+M_b/\\beta)C_IT+\\beta^{-1}\\bigl(2C_P+[2\\nu\\sqrt T+C_c(M_E+\\sqrt T M_u)]\\nu^{-1/2}\\bigr)C_*+\\beta^{-1}(2\\nu T+2C_cT).$$\nFor every $\\xi\\in Q$, every $\\eta\\in C_c^\\infty(0,T)$, and every node $0\\le m\\le N$, the interface observations satisfy\n$$\\left|\\bigl(P(t_m)-P_h^m,\\xi\\bigr)_{L^2}\\right|\\le KH\\|\\xi\\|_Q.$$\n\n$$\\left|\\left(\\int_0^T(p(t)-\\bar p_h(t))\\eta(t)\\,dt,\\xi\\right)_{L^2}\\right|\\le(K+1)H\\|\\eta'\\|_{L^1(0,T)}\\|\\xi\\|_Q.$$\nThese are accumulated-pressure and time-tested pressure bounds on the smooth branch. They do not assert an instantaneous pressure-error rate.",
