          "title": "Weak velocity limits do not supply the smooth pressure-observation estimate",
          "statement": "Assume both Countable Choice and the Axiom of Choice. Let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$, $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$, be a nonempty bounded connected Lipschitz polyhedral domain, let $0<T<\\infty$, let $\\nu>0$, let $V=H^1_0(D;\\mathbb R^d)$, $Q=L^2_0(D)$, $V_\\sigma=\\{v\\in V:\\operatorname{div}v=0\\}$, and $H_\\sigma=\\overline{V_\\sigma}^{\\,L^2(D)^d}$. Define $\\varepsilon(v)=(\\nabla v+\\nabla v^{\\mathsf T})/2$, $a_\\nu(v,w)=2\\nu\\int_D\\varepsilon(v):\\varepsilon(w)\\,dx$, $b(v,q)=-\\int_Dq\\,\\operatorname{div}v\\,dx$, and $c(a;v,w)=\\tfrac12\\int_D((a\\cdot\\nabla)v\\cdot w-(a\\cdot\\nabla)w\\cdot v)\\,dx$. On each matching shape-regular affine simplicial mesh, let $V_{h,j}$ be the MINI continuous piecewise-linear velocity space enriched by one interior bubble per simplex and let $Q_{h,j}$ be the continuous piecewise-linear pressure space with zero mean. Set $Z_j=\\{v_{h,j}\\in V_{h,j}:b(v_{h,j},q_{h,j})=0\\text{ for every }q_{h,j}\\in Q_{h,j}\\}$. Take $f\\in L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)$ and $u_0\\in H_\\sigma$. Use a mesh family with maximum cell diameters $h_j\\to0$ and time partitions $0=t_0^j<\\cdots<t_{N_j}^j=T$ whose maximum steps $\\tau_{\\max,j}$ tend to zero, without a relation between these limits. On each mesh, initialize by the $L^2$ projection of $u_0$ onto $Z_j$ and choose any actual mixed backward Euler MINI solution; write $\\bar u_j(t)=u_j^n$ on $(t_{n-1}^j,t_n^j]$. A subsequence satisfies $\\bar u_j\\to u$ strongly in $L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)$ and weakly in $L^2(0,T;V)$, where $u\\in L^\\infty(0,T;H_\\sigma)\\cap L^2(0,T;V_\\sigma)$ is weakly continuous into $H_\\sigma$, has $u(0)=u_0$, and obeys, for every fixed $v\\in V_\\sigma$ and $\\eta\\in C^1([0,T])$ vanishing near $T$,\n$$-\\int_0^T(u(t),v)_{L^2}\\eta'(t)\\,dt+\\int_0^T\\bigl(a_\\nu(u(t),v)+c(u(t);u(t),v)\\bigr)\\eta(t)\\,dt=\\int_0^T(f(t),v)_{L^2}\\eta(t)\\,dt+(u_0,v)_{L^2}\\eta(0),$$\nand, for almost every $t\\in(0,T)$,\n$$\\frac12\\|u(t)\\|_{L^2}^2+\\nu\\int_0^t\\|\\nabla u(s)\\|_{L^2}^2\\,ds\\le\\frac12\\|u_0\\|_{L^2}^2+\\int_0^t(f(s),u(s))_{L^2}\\,ds.$$\nThe subsequential-limit theorem does not assert pressure regularity or a pressure-observation error estimate. The accumulated-pressure observation proposition on this page additionally requires the strong no-slip regularity $u\\in W^{1,\\infty}(0,T;H^2(D)^d\\cap V_\\sigma)$ and $p\\in W^{1,\\infty}(0,T;H^1(D)\\cap Q)$. Thus the weak-limit theorem alone does not supply that pressure estimate. This scope remark does not assert that a pressure is absent or rule out a separately proved pressure-primitive result.",
